  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">AUC,Gender Peace and Security JFA, GPSP 2015-16 - AUC/PSD Gender JFA</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">AUC,Gender Peace and Security JFA, GPSP 2015-16</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Gender Peace and Security&#xa0;Programme (GPSP) aims at mainstreaming gender into the African Peace and Security Architecture (APSA) and improving the quality and effectiveness of mechanisms and institutions in charge of preventing violence, including sexual and gender-based violence, and addressing issues of protection of civilians in conflict and post-conflict situations.
It has 4 main objectives;&#xa0;
Outcome 1: To enhance the Capacities of African Institutions Working in the Areas of Peace and Security and Human Rights to Mainstream Gender into the Continental Peace and Security Agenda.
Outcome2: To strengthen advocacy efforts, Partnership and promoting research and dialogue on Gender, Peace and Security.
Outcome 3: To strengthen Women&apos;s roles in peace and security in Africa.
Outcome 4: To prevent and respond to vulnerabilities of women, men, and children in time of conflict and post-conflict situations, and ending impunity.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">Insatsen best&#xe5;r av ett st&#xf6;d till Gender, Peace and Security programmet (GPSP), som ligger under AUC:s avdelning f&#xf6;r fred och s&#xe4;kerhet (Department for Peace and Security). Programmet har som m&#xe5;ls&#xe4;ttning att integrera j&#xe4;mlikhet i den Afrikanska Fred- och S&#xe4;kerhetsarkitekturen (APSA) och att f&#xf6;rb&#xe4;ttra kvaliteten och effektiviteten hos de institutioner och mekanismer som ansvarar f&#xf6;r att f&#xf6;rhindra v&#xe5;ld, inklusive sexuellt- och genusgrundat v&#xe5;ld, och att addresera fr&#xe5;gor r&#xf6;rande att skydda civila i konflikt- och postkonflikt situationer. 

 Insatsen bed&#xf6;ms vidare ha tillr&#xe4;ckligt goda planer f&#xf6;r att tillfredsst&#xe4;llande genomf&#xf6;ra sina planer, och en tillr&#xe4;ckligt god kapacitet till att genomf&#xf6;ra uppf&#xf6;ljning av aktiviteter inom programmet. Dessutom bed&#xf6;ms insatsens budget och finansiering vara tillfyllest f&#xf6;r att Sida ska besluta att st&#xf6;dja insatsen.</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The programme will contribute towards policy development and debate   in the field of gender, peace and security and protection with a view to contributing towards more coordinated programming in this area by  the AU, the UN, the RECs, INGO, CSOs and other multi-lateral and      bi-lateral partners working on these issues in Africa.</narrative>
  </description>
